{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966805,"nonce":"ISyoVRYOKbcwN8mubyecrtT8VLk=","title":"SchedulerHandle::with_timeline woke on every access including pure reads, so painting a","message":"`SchedulerHandle::with_timeline` takes `FnOnce(\u0026mut Timeline)`, so it cannot\ntell a read from a mutation and wakes unconditionally on any successful\naccess. Every pure reader (`value`, `progress`, `entry_progress`,\n`has_entries`, `entry_ids`) went through it.\n\nThat made *reading* a redraw signal. The paint walk samples a spinner's\nrotation via `MotionState::get_rotation` -\u003e `AnimatedTimeline::get` -\u003e\n`with_timeline` -\u003e wake callback -\u003e `frame_dirty = true`. Drawing re-armed\nthe next frame, so the loop could never park: no visibility gate, no FPS\ncap, and no dirty check can break a cycle that the act of painting creates.\nSymptom was an idle window at 25-40% CPU with nothing moving on screen.\n\nFixed by `with_timeline_read` (`FnOnce(\u0026Timeline)`, no wake) for the\nobserving queries; seek/start/mutators keep the waking path. Measured on\ncn_playground: 17-21% idle -\u003e 0%, one frame entry total. A visible spinner\nstill drives frames (~17%), so on-screen animation is unaffected.\n\nSecond, smaller leak in the same hunt: `needs_vsync` (cap bypass) and\n`needs_motion_redraw` (feeds `any_redraw_signal`) in the windowed frame loop\nread the ungated `has_active_motions`, counting motions on nodes the paint\nwalk never reached. Both now use `has_active_motions_visible`. Worth 17-21%\n-\u003e 11-12% on its own.\n\nDebugging lesson: the frame gate said `did_rebuild=false needs_relayout=false\nneeds_vsync=false` while frames kept arriving, and `stateful::request_redraw`\nfired exactly once. What finally named it was a one-shot\n`Backtrace::force_capture()` inside the wake callback at call #400. Reach for\nthat far earlier than subsystem-by-subsystem elimination. Also: a\nrate-limited log with an EVEN modulus aliases against a period-2 alternation\nand reports only one phase; use an odd modulus or plain counters.\n\nRelated: gotcha spinner pinned text collect,\ngotcha scrollbar spring spin, gotcha fast path visible anim latch.","files":null}]}